  "solution": {
    "text": "Critical temperature is the temperature at and above which gases cannot liquefied, no matter how much pressure is applied. For Z gas of given gases, critical temperature is highest<br /><br /><math> <mrow>  <msub>   <mtext>T</mtext>   <mtext>c</mtext>  </msub>  <mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mfrac>   <mrow>    <mtext>8a</mtext></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>27Rb</mtext></mrow>  </mfrac>  <mo>&#x21D2;</mo><msub>   <mtext>T</mtext>   <mtext>c</mtext>  </msub>  <mo>&#x221D;</mo><mfrac>   <mtext>a</mtext>   <mtext>b</mtext>  </mfrac>  <mo>&#x21D2;</mo></mrow></math>It is highest for <math> <mtext>Z</mtext></math><br />",
